    "body": "Stanley Druckenmiller. ( Screenshot from Bloomberg TV | YouTube. )\nBy: Staff Writer November 17, 2026\nBillionaire investor Stanley Druckenmiller said Tuesday he was betting on a drop in copper prices, a day after his family office disclosed new stakes in three gold producers. The shares were worth $129.1 million (C$184.6 million) at Sept. 30 closing prices.\nDuquesne Family Office held 380,400 shares of Newmont (NYSE, ASX: NEM) worth $43.9 million, 1,054,600 shares of Barrick Mining (TSX: ABX; NYSE: B) worth $42.9 million and 231,050 shares of Agnico Eagle Mines (TSX, NYSE: AEM) worth $42.3 million, according to its quarterly filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission.\nDruckenmiller described his copper short at the TomorrowX investment conference in Austin, Texas, where he said his priority was preserving capital , Barron’s reported. He cautioned that the U.S. economy could disappoint in the second half of 2027, CoinDesk reported.\nThe three gold producers accounted for 2.9% of the $4.5 billion in securities Duquesne disclosed at the end of September. Three industrial-metals holdings worth a combined $70.7 million at the end of June had dropped off its filing.\nSouthern Copper, Cliffs\nDuquesne’s June filing listed 123,060 shares of Southern Copper (NYSE: SCCO) worth $21.4 million, 4.2 million shares of steelmaker Cleveland-Cliffs (NYSE: CLF) worth $39.6 million and 185,640 shares of aluminum producer Alcoa (NYSE: AA) worth $9.7 million.\nDuquesne kept its 300,200 shares of Skeena Gold & Silver (TSX, NYSE: SKE), which is developing the Eskay Creek gold-silver project in British Columbia. The $8.9-million stake brought the four gold holdings to 3.1% of the September total.\nThe family office also increased its holding of Argentine oil and gas producer YPF (NYSE: YPF) by 13% to about 3.5 million American depositary shares worth $177.6 million. Genetic testing company Natera (Nasdaq: NTRA) remained its largest disclosed holding at 29% of the total.\nTwo other managers added to individual gold stocks. Sprott (TSX, NYSE: SII) increased its Barrick stake by 49% to 1.3 million shares. Tudor Investment more than doubled its Newmont common shares to 739,545 from 318,054. Tudor also held Newmont put options covering 250,400 shares and calls on 21,000 shares.\nDuquesne listed 65 entries at Sept. 30, down from 95 worth $5.2 billion at June 30. Form 13F gives a quarter-end snapshot. It omits short positions and trade prices, and values options using the underlying shares. Print\nCOMMODITY: Copper Gold Iron Ore\nREGION: Canada United States\nCOMPANY: Agnico Eagle Mines Alcoa Barrick Mining Cleveland Cliffs Newmont Skeena Gold and Silver Southern Copper Sprott YPF\nRepublish this article",
